  "tagline": "Lisp-built RDF and document knowledge graph with vector store, reasoning and LLM agents.",
  "description": "AllegroGraph from Franz Inc. is a commercial RDF triplestore that also stores JSON-LD documents and vector embeddings, positioned as a neuro-symbolic AI platform. It supports SPARQL 1.1, Prolog rules, RDFS++ reasoning, SHACL, geospatial and temporal queries, and FedShard for distributing a knowledge graph across shards. Version 9.0 (May 2026) introduced GraphTalker, an agent that iteratively writes and runs SPARQL from natural language, and 9.1 followed in October 2026. It suits enterprises building knowledge graphs with heavy reasoning or LLM integration; the free edition is capped at a few million triples.",
